  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to the Mpox epidemic in the DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is aiming at, by March 2026 improving access to Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) by providing life -saving WASH support to approximately 100,000 people affected by the M -Pox outbreak in North Kivu, South Kivu and Equateur Provices. Oxfam will be working with communities through Community Health Volunteers and with its implementation in the region, it will be easy to reactivate and train Community Health Volunteers for this particular project for awareness -raising campaigns and, at the same time, identification of the most vulnerable households in order to provide them with NFI kits and also provide WaSH kits to health structures in the areas affected by the epidemic.</narrative>
  </description>
